{{!--
Rows by tag, under « Les plus lus » (the markup is in rows-body.hbs). The sequence of forms is fixed by the
theme so that two neighbouring rows never share a form (Final-rangees-catalogue):
  1. shelf of 16:9 tiles   (row 1)          4. numbered text list, by date   (row 3)
  2. tag tiles « Tags » (most used tags) 5. collection banner             (row 4)
  3. 2:3 posters           (row 2)          6. one large post + four          (row 5)
Which tag fills each row: the theme setting « Home row N » (home_row_1 ... home_row_5, a tag slug,
Ghost Admin > Settings > Design > Homepage) when it is set; otherwise the Nth most used public tag.
A setting naming no existing public tag (e.g. "none") removes its row; a tag without posts has no row.
A tag pinned by one row never fills another: when the Nth most used tag is pinned in a setting (any row),
the row that would fall back on it is left out, so no tag appears twice (and every id row-<slug> is unique).
The five most used tags are queried once, and only when a row has no setting; each row without setting
takes its place in that one result. A row with a setting queries its own tag.
--}}
{{#match (concat "," @custom.home_row_1 "," @custom.home_row_2 "," @custom.home_row_3 "," @custom.home_row_4 "," @custom.home_row_5 ",") "~" ",,"}}
  {{!-- The block of {{#get}} changes the context: {{#with ..}} gives it back --}}
  {{#get "tags" filter="visibility:public" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="5" as |toptags|}}{{#with ..}}
    {{> "home/rows-body" toptags=toptags}}
  {{/with}}{{/get}}
{{else}}
  {{> "home/rows-body"}}
{{/match}}
